  "notes": "snapshot.js now decides visibility per text node for page text, headings and selection. A node is kept only if its client rects survive ancestor overflow clipping along its containing-block chain, the legacy clip property and clip-path inset, keep at least 2px in each direction, stay inside the document (catches text-indent and negative offsets), have a non-transparent text colour, and are not under an opaque element at the rect centre when that point is in the viewport. Not covered, now stated in docs/assist/03: low-contrast colour, fonts of 2px or more, occlusion outside the viewport, overlays with pointer-events:none. Text in the viewport currently covered by a solid sticky header is also dropped, deliberately failing safe. Fail-before was proven by temporarily restoring the 2de591e snapshot.js in this tree (2 failed), then the repaired file (2 passed), because creating a separate worktree was denied. Full tests/assist and tests/web: 2631 passed.",
